# Flixbox starter Caddyfile — copy to ${CONFIG_DIR}/caddy/Caddyfile
# Enable with: COMPOSE_PROFILES=proxy (or ./bin/flixbox up proxy)
#
# Default: LAN virtual hosts on port 80 (HTTP).
# For public HTTPS, replace domain prefixes with your public FQDN (e.g. jellyfin.yourdomain.com)
# and Caddy will automatically manage Let's Encrypt / ZeroSSL TLS certificates on port 443.
#
# WARNING: This file has NO authentication. Do not publish :80/:443 to the WAN without a
# separate auth layer (SSO is out of v0.1 baseline). Prefer LAN-only or a hardened reverse proxy you control.
# Homepage has no login; Seerr/Jellyfin auth alone is not a substitute for edge access control.

http://{$JELLYFIN_DOMAIN:jellyfin.local} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy jellyfin:8096
}

http://{$SEERR_DOMAIN:requests.local} {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy seerr:5055
}

:80 {
	encode gzip
	reverse_proxy homepage:3000
}
